  "Question": "\\(\\log125\\) equals:",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(100\\log1.25\\)",
    "B": "\\(5\\log3\\)",
    "C": "\\(3\\log25\\)",
    "D": "\\(3-3\\log2\\)",
    "E": "\\((\\log25)(\\log5)\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "D",
  "Solution": "Here \\(\\log\\) denotes the common logarithm, with base \\(10\\). To express the answer using \\(\\log2\\), write \\(125=(10/2)^3\\). The power and quotient rules give\n\\[\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\log125\n&=3\\log\\left(\\frac{10}{2}\\right)\\\\\n&=3(\\log10-\\log2)\\\\\n&=\\boxed{3-3\\log2},\n\\end{aligned}\n\\]\nsince \\(\\log10=1\\). The answer is \\(\\boxed{\\text{D}}\\).",
